      <!--

    ************************ FeatureViewer ************************

    A Feature is its geometry drawn (through the editor's AdaptiveViewer, which dispatches by the
    geometry's runtime type - a Point gets the pin) with EVERY attribute listed under it, one Row
    of key and value per attribute, sorted by name, the value cell through the editor's
    AdaptiveViewer (a boolean is a checkbox) - what a GIS shows when you click a feature.
    Not the editor's DictionaryViewer: that one stops at the TooltipNumberOfItemsOfCollection
    setting, 3 rows by default, and prints '...' for the rest.
-->
